timeline.body:
@normanmaurer 
This is rather uncomplete: `HttpResponseEncoder` should check against many concrete types that can be produced by users (almost all default netty http response-related types, including content(s)), but this one is a widely adopted one, hence should be enough.

Users not satisfied can still override this method and provide the checks based on the types they believe are more common among their users (including custom types). wdyt?

